  "usage": {
    "status": "verified",
    "verifiedAt": "2026-06-08",
    "resultPull": "poll",
    "auth": "siwx",
    "callShape": "POST https://stablesocial.dev/api/reddit/post-comments with JSON body {post_id, max_comments?, order_by?, max_page_size?, cursor?} (x402-paid ~$0.06). Returns HTTP 202 async job. Then GET the returned pollUrl with SIWX auth from the SAME wallet that paid until body.status===\"finished\".",
    "inputExample": {
      "post_id": "1g5z3kq",
      "max_comments": 1
    },
    "outputShape": "POST -> body.jobId, body.pollUrl, body.token, body.status (pending). Poll (GET pollUrl, SIWX) -> body.status (pending|finished), comments at body.data.items[], pagination at body.data.page_info.{cursor,has_next_page}.",
    "quirks": [
      "Required field is post_id (the Reddit post ID like '1g5z3kq', NOT a full URL).",
      "POST returns HTTP 202 async job (jobId+pollUrl+token, status=pending) — the comments are NOT in the POST response.",
      "The pollUrl REQUIRES SIWX wallet auth from the SAME wallet that paid; a plain unauthenticated GET returns 402 'SIWX authentication required'.",
      "Poll with SIWX (qa-pay --siwx GET pollUrl) — polling is free (no extra charge). Loop until body.status==='finished'.",
      "Result comments live at body.data.items[] on the finished poll response, not in the POST body.",
      "max_comments caps at 300 (use a small value like 1 to keep responses light); only post_id is required.",
      "Job can finish with data.items:[] if the post has no fetchable comments / is old or removed — empty result is not an error (status still 'finished')."
    ],
    "needs": [],
    "needsApproval": false,
    "guide": "POST to https://stablesocial.dev/api/reddit/post-comments with JSON {\"post_id\":\"<reddit post id, e.g. 1g5z3kq>\",\"max_comments\":N}; this is x402-paid (~$0.06) and returns a 202 async job containing jobId, pollUrl, token, status:pending. Then GET the returned pollUrl using SIWX authentication signed by the SAME wallet that paid (an unauthenticated poll fails with 'SIWX authentication required'); polling is free. Repeat the poll until body.status === \"finished\", then read the comments from body.data.items[] and paginate via body.data.page_info.cursor if has_next_page is true.",
    "costObservedUsd": 0.06
  },
